From: Riley <oreo4455@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rotation-manager: rotate the lock screen as well

Phosh keeps the lock screen still and forces it to portrait on phones, where its
keypad didn't fit in landscape. The L16's lock screen fits (with the compact
keypad) and the camera is held in landscape: let it follow the sensor, as phrog's
login screen (Phosh locked for good) then does too.
---
--- a/src/rotation-manager.c	2026-10-05 10:42:57.042091084 -0700
+++ b/src/rotation-manager.c	2026-10-05 10:46:25.898728644 -0700
@@ -118,8 +118,8 @@
     return TRUE;
   }
 
+  /* L16: the lock screen follows the sensor too (see fixup_lockscreen_orientation) */
   if (self->orientation_locked || !self->claimed ||
-      phosh_lockscreen_manager_get_locked (self->lockscreen_manager) ||
       self->mode == PHOSH_ROTATION_MANAGER_MODE_OFF)
     return FALSE;
 
@@ -262,6 +262,10 @@
 
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_MODE_MANAGER (mode_manager));
 
+  /* L16: the lock screen works in landscape (lockscreen-compact-keypad.patch) and the
+   * camera is held in landscape, so the lock screen rotates as the rest of the shell */
+  return;
+
   if (!self->monitor)
     return;
 
